{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he called it Shevah.</b> He called the well Shevah because it was the seventh place in which they dug a well. Three of Abraham's, which the Philistines stopped up, as it says: <b>and all the wells... the Philistines had stopped them up</b> — and <b>all</b> would not be said for fewer than three; and three of Isaac's, which are Esek, Sitnah, and Rehovot; and this was the seventh, which they called Shevah." "<b>Therefore the name of the city is Be'er Sheva.</b> With a segol, indicating both the oath and the number seven; but in Abraham's days the name of the city was Be'er Shava with a qamatz, after the oath alone."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:53.605699393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}